{"seeAlsoSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/VStack","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/HStack","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Spacer","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/RenderCycle"],"title":"Related Documentation","anchor":"Related-Documentation"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StateManagement","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ThemingGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/FocusSystem","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/StatusBarGuide","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/AppearanceAndColors","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Preferences","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/CustomViews","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/KeyboardShortcuts","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/PaletteReference","doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/ListAndTable"],"title":"Guides","generated":true,"anchor":"Guides"}],"metadata":{"title":"Layout System","modules":[{"name":"TUIkit"}],"roleHeading":"Article","role":"article"},"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/LayoutSystem"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit"]]},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Understand the two-pass layout used by stacks and other layout containers."}],"sections":[],"kind":"article","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"Overview"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"TUIkit uses a two-pass layout system inspired by SwiftUI’s layout protocol. Layout containers like ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/VStack","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" and ","type":"text"},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/HStack","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":" first ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"measure"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" each child, then ","type":"text"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"render","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" them with allocated sizes. This approach enables features like flexible spacers, proportional sizing, and proper alignment.","type":"text"}]},{"text":"The Two Passes","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"The-Two-Passes"},{"text":"Pass 1: Measure","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Pass-1-Measure"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The parent proposes a size to each child via ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ProposedSize"},{"text":". Each child responds with a ","type":"text"},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ViewSize"},{"text":" that describes how much space it needs and whether it can flex.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["Parent (VStack)","  ├─ propose(width: 40, height: nil) → Text    → ViewSize(10, 1, flexible: false)","  ├─ propose(width: 40, height: nil) → Spacer  → ViewSize(0, 0, flexible: true)","  └─ propose(width: 40, height: nil) → Button  → ViewSize(12, 1, flexible: false)"],"syntax":null},{"text":"Pass 2: Render","level":3,"type":"heading","anchor":"Pass-2-Render"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"After measuring all children, the parent distributes the remaining space among flexible children and renders each child with its final allocated size."}]},{"type":"codeListing","code":["Parent allocates:","  Text   → render(width: 40, height: 1)   \/\/ Gets full width, fixed height","  Spacer → render(width: 40, height: 8)   \/\/ Gets remaining vertical space","  Button → render(width: 40, height: 1)   \/\/ Gets full width, fixed height"],"syntax":null},{"text":"ProposedSize","level":2,"type":"heading","anchor":"ProposedSize"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"code":"ProposedSize","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" represents the space a parent offers to a child. Either dimension can be "},{"code":"nil","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":", meaning “use your ideal size.”"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public struct ProposedSize {","    public var width: Int?","    public var height: Int?","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"header":"row","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Value","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Meaning"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Use ideal size (no constraint)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"0"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Minimum size"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"> 0"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Available space in characters\/lines","type":"text"}]}]]],"type":"table"},{"text":"ViewSize","anchor":"ViewSize","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"ViewSize","type":"codeVoice"},{"type":"text","text":" is the child’s response: how much space it needs and whether it can expand."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["public struct ViewSize {","    public var width: Int","    public var height: Int","    public var isWidthFlexible: Bool","    public var isHeightFlexible: Bool","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Factory methods make common patterns concise:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["ViewSize.fixed(20, 1)                    \/\/ Fixed 20x1, won't expand","ViewSize.flexible(minWidth: 0, minHeight: 0)  \/\/ Expands in both directions","ViewSize.flexibleWidth(minWidth: 5, height: 1) \/\/ Expands horizontally only"],"type":"codeListing"},{"text":"The Layoutable Protocol","anchor":"The-Layoutable-Protocol","level":2,"type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Views that participate in two-pass layout conform to "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Layoutable"},{"type":"text","text":" (which extends "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Renderable"},{"type":"text","text":"):"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","code":["protocol Layoutable: Renderable {","    func sizeThatFits(proposal: ProposedSize, context: RenderContext) -> ViewSize","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"A default implementation renders the view and measures the resulting buffer. Custom implementations can calculate size without rendering for better performance.","type":"text"}]},{"level":2,"text":"ChildView","type":"heading","anchor":"ChildView"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Layout containers wrap their children in ","type":"text"},{"code":"ChildView","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", which provides a uniform interface for measuring and rendering:","type":"text"}]},{"syntax":"swift","code":["struct ChildView {","    func measure(proposal: ProposedSize, context: RenderContext) -> ViewSize","    func render(width: Int, height: Int, context: RenderContext) -> FrameBuffer","}"],"type":"codeListing"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"codeVoice","code":"ChildView"},{"type":"text","text":" automatically detects spacers and propagates child identity for correct state management."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"How Stacks Lay Out Children","type":"heading","anchor":"How-Stacks-Lay-Out-Children","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/VStack","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" and "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/HStack","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" follow this algorithm:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"type":"orderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Measure","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" all children with the parent’s proposed size"}]}]},{"content":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Sum"}]},{"type":"text","text":" the fixed sizes along the stack axis"}],"type":"paragraph"}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"strong","inlineContent":[{"text":"Distribute","type":"text"}]},{"text":" remaining space among flexible children (spacers, flexible text fields, etc.)","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Render"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" each child with its allocated size","type":"text"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Compose","type":"text"}],"type":"strong"},{"text":" the rendered buffers with the specified spacing and alignment","type":"text"}]}]}]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Flexible children share remaining space equally. If multiple spacers exist, they each get an equal portion of the leftover space."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Which Views Are Layoutable?","type":"heading","anchor":"Which-Views-Are-Layoutable","level":2},{"header":"row","type":"table","rows":[[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"View"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Layoutable?"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Flexibility","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Text","isActive":true,"type":"reference"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Yes"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Fixed (wraps at proposed width)","type":"text"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Spacer","type":"reference","isActive":true}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Yes","type":"text"}]}],[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Flexible in stack direction"}]}]],[[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/TUIkit\/documentation\/TUIkit\/Button"}]}],[{"type"